course: dictionary
lesson: 1996
title: Hiding and keeping secret: conceal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To conceal something is to hide it so that it cannot be seen or found. It is a more formal word than hide, so you will meet it in stories, reports and rules. «Whoever conceals their sins does not prosper, but the one who confesses and renounces them finds mercy» (Proverbs 28:13).
explain: The clues in that sentence help you. Conceals is set against confesses, so the person who conceals their sins is keeping them hidden instead of owning up to them. Try the swap: «Whoever hides their sins does not prosper» still makes sense, so hide is a good match for conceal.
explain: Conceal can also mean keeping a feeling or a fact secret. «She could barely conceal her delight» means she was trying to hide how happy she was, but her grin gave it away. If anyone asks you to conceal a secret that makes you feel unsafe, always tell a trusted adult.
fact: Conceal is a verb, so it changes: conceals, concealed, concealing.
fact: «Conceal» means to hide something so that it cannot be seen or found.
fact: «Conceal» can also mean to keep a feeling or a fact secret.
fact: Animals can conceal themselves with camouflage, blending in with their surroundings.
fact: Hide is a simpler word you can use in place of conceal in most sentences.
exercise: «The chameleon tried to conceal itself against the green leaves.» What does conceal mean here? | To paint itself bright red | To make a loud noise | *To hide, so that it cannot be seen | To fly high into the trees
exercise: Find and copy one word from the Proverbs sentence that means to own up to something. | prosper | mercy | *confesses | conceals
exercise: «Mia could barely conceal her delight when she opened the present.» What does conceal mean in this sentence? | To show everyone loudly | *To keep the feeling hidden | To tear the paper off | To forget about the present
test: «The thief tried to conceal the stolen jewels under his coat.» What does conceal mean? | To show them proudly | To count them carefully | To sell them quickly | *To hide so they cannot be seen
test: Which word is the past tense of conceal? | concealing | concealer | conceals | *concealed
exam: What does conceal mean in «He tried to conceal his tears from his sister»? | To hand them over to a teacher | To shout about them loudly | To wipe them away with a tissue | *To keep them hidden from being seen
